My younger sister Sofía comes on the screen.
She sits near my mother.
"Sister, what is in your hand?" she asks.
I take a small box.
It is a bakery box.
I open that box.
There is a sweet in it.
I show it to the camera.
"Its name is halwa," I tell her.
This is a good snack.
"Who makes that?" Sofía asks.
"A bakery in Kochi," I say.
This halwa has a nice red color.
"Does it have good sweetness?" she asks.
"Yes, it has a good taste," I reply.
I eat a small piece.
There is a lot of happiness on her face.
I also like this sweet very much.
